    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule to skip public holidays in `ResolveRegistrationDate.java` (the one place that resolves and rolls the registration date; downstream steps \u2014 daily-registration count, owner stamping, membership number \u2014 all consume the published value, so they inherit the fix automatically).\n\n**What changed** in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/ResolveRegistrationDate.java`:\n- Added a `HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed 2026 dates (`2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`).\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay` from fixed `+2`/`+1` weekend offsets to a **loop** that rolls forward one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, or a listed holiday. This correctly handles chained cases (e.g. `2026-12-25` Fri \u2192 `12-26`/`12-27` weekend \u2192 `12-28` holiday \u2192 `12-29`).\n\nThis mirrors the reference `toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` already present in the test base (`AcceptanceBase.java`). The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
