    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change lands entirely in the unit that already owns this concern. `ResolveRegistrationDate` already resolved the effective date and rolled it onto a business day via a private-ish `toBusinessDay` helper; extending that same helper to also skip holidays is exactly where a maintainer would look and reach for.\n\n- The `HOLIDAYS` constant sits next to the only logic that consumes it, package-private `static final` so tests in the same package can reach it \u2014 consistent with `toBusinessDay` being package-private for the same reason.\n- Replacing the two `if` branches with a single `while` loop is the natural way to express \"roll forward until we hit a real business day,\" and it correctly generalizes the old weekend-only behavior rather than bolting a second holiday-specific block alongside it (which would have been the duplication risk here).\n- No DTO leakage or responsibility creep: the class still just resolves and publishes the date; the doc comment on both the class and the helper was updated to match.\n\nNothing to improve structurally.",
